WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.167
-Mother's Day is this weekend,
and with today being

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.067
Teacher Appreciation Day,
we wanted to do something --

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
...special

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.501
in honor of that.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.501
So we teamed up with Samsung
to surprise some amazing

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.667
moms out there,
moms who are also teachers.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.200
And we brought them to
New York

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.567
and told them that they were
going to appear

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.367
in a Mother's Day special
to air on NBC.

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.734
What they didn't know is that
I was hiding nearby

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.634
and about to surprise them
with a very special

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.567
Mother's Day gift from Samsung.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.968
Check this out.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.934
[ Applause ]

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:33.067
♪♪

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.234
-Hi, my name is Susan.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.801
I'm here to talk about
my wonderful friend,

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.334
teacher-mom extraordinaire,
Joanne.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:42.667
She teaches high school on the
Upper East Side in Manhattan.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.434
She grew up in the Philippines,

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.234
and she didn't have
a lot of money growing up,

00:00:46.234 --> 00:00:49.033
and I think that that's sort of
what makes her who she is.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.567
She wants to give back.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.667
Joanne is someone who
doesn't' believe that

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.133
teaching and learning
stays in a classroom.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.400
She's always bringing
her kids out into the world.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.434
Somehow, in between all of that,

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.067
she's the mom that keeps
all of our friends together.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.334
And she always just makes us
feel super loved.

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:09.467
-My amazing mother is a teacher
and a wonderful mom.

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.634
My mother immigrated
to the United States

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.100
close to 40 years ago.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.434
Throughout my mom's career
as an educator,

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.167
she has helped many children.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:22.234
Her drive is working with
students who have immigrated

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:25.200
from other countries,
inspiring all of her students

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.734
that we come from
all walks of life.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.934
-My mom raised me
as a single mother.

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.501
She's always worked really hard

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.634
to provide a really good
life for me just by herself.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.100
She decided she wanted to
go back to school.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.300
She was substitute teaching
and said,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.901
"I want to do better and provide
better for these kids."

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.634
And here she is today,
a teacher of 4th grade

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.501
in a low-income school district,
and she's great at it.

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:50.667
She's also helping my cousin
raise her son with her

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.968
so she can go to school.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.100
And now I'm gonna cry.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.300
But she is awesome.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.601
[ Voice breaking ] She's the
best mom anyone could ask for.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:00.100
-Hi. Good morning.
-Hi, how are you doing?

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.033
Thanks for coming in.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:02.434
-Thanks for having us.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.868
-So we're just gonna record some
lines for this NBC special.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.334
So they're on the prompter.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:08.167
Whenever you're ready.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:10.100
And...action.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.501
-Hi, I'm Susan from
Long Island City, New York.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.467
-And I'm Joanne from Astoria.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.033
-And we want to wish
all the amazing moms watching

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.334
a happy Mother's Day.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:20.767
-Samsung heard all about me
and wants to thank me

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.834
for all I do as a mother
and teacher

00:02:22.834 --> 00:02:26.868
